/*Q24.
Imagine a fun Chocolate Shop where a friendly Choco-Maker wants to know how much a chocolate treat costs. They have a special tool called the Chocolate Calculator. When kids pick their chocolates, the Choco-Maker puts in how many and the price for each. Your task is to make a program that quickly figures out how much the chocolates cost altogether.

Input format:
  - The first line is the number of chocolates a kid wants (a whole number).
  - The second line is the cost of one chocolate (a number with decimals).

Output format:
  - The result is the total cost of all the chocolates (a number with one decimal number).

Note: A partial code is provided in the editor.*/
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*Logic: The problem asks for one decimal place, so use %.1f.*/

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int count = sc.nextInt();
        double cost = sc.nextDouble();
        System.out.printf("%.1f%n", count * cost);
        sc.close();
    }
}
